Upstream-Status: Pending
Exit: Drop alongside 0010 when fdsdk resolves version detection for hatch-vcs-backed packages in the sandbox.
Subject: python3-chardet: use UNQUALIFIED PRETEND_VERSION env vars

Build r2p77 shows the per-dist-name env vars from 0010 arriving in the
sandbox (log: "SETUPTOOLS_SCM_PRETEND_VERSION_FOR_CHARDET: 6.0.0" and
"VCS_VERSIONING_PRETEND_VERSION_FOR_CHARDET: 6.0.0") — but they are
not consulted. vcs_versioning._get_version_impl still runs
git describe --match '*[0-9]*' (note the generic pattern, not
chardet-specific) and hits the 40s subprocess timeout. hatchling's
error-formatting path then crashes with TypeError when trying to
re-raise TimeoutExpired.

Something in the hatch-vcs -> setuptools-scm -> vcs_versioning handoff
drops the dist-name match. Add the UNQUALIFIED env vars — they apply
globally regardless of the dist name passed in. Safe because chardet
is the only package built inside this element.

diff --git a/elements/components/python3-chardet.bst b/elements/components/python3-chardet.bst
--- a/elements/components/python3-chardet.bst
+++ b/elements/components/python3-chardet.bst
@@ -1,6 +1,8 @@
 environment:
   # setuptools-scm#957 workaround: skip VCS version detection in sandbox.
+  SETUPTOOLS_SCM_PRETEND_VERSION: "6.0.0"
+  VCS_VERSIONING_PRETEND_VERSION: "6.0.0"
   SETUPTOOLS_SCM_PRETEND_VERSION_FOR_CHARDET: "6.0.0"
   VCS_VERSIONING_PRETEND_VERSION_FOR_CHARDET: "6.0.0"

